WEBVTT

00:01.696 --> 00:04.449
[Takemichi] <i>I started thinking. What if…</i>

00:05.158 --> 00:06.493
<i>after I change the future,</i>

00:07.410 --> 00:11.664
<i>someone else comes in
and changes it again, same as I do?</i>

00:11.665 --> 00:13.249
<i>I wonder…</i>

00:13.250 --> 00:16.127
<i>Maybe Kisaki can travel through time
like me.</i>

00:17.420 --> 00:19.089
Takemitchy…

00:19.589 --> 00:20.590
Huh?

00:21.591 --> 00:23.510
Take care of Mikey…

00:24.594 --> 00:26.680
for me, 'kay?

00:31.810 --> 00:37.566
In the end, I'm not related to Shinichiro
or to Emma or Mikey or anybody.

00:38.733 --> 00:40.193
There it is, Mikey.

00:41.319 --> 00:42.403
What now?

00:42.404 --> 00:44.114
Don't wanna save me?

00:45.365 --> 00:46.533
[grunts]

00:49.452 --> 00:52.288
You're not getting away! Don't you dare!

00:52.289 --> 00:55.500
I'm not letting you go back to the future
ever again, Kisaki!

00:58.086 --> 00:59.087
[chuckles]

01:00.630 --> 01:03.424
"Back to the future" you said. Really?

01:03.425 --> 01:04.549
Huh?

01:04.550 --> 01:09.179
I see. You're trying to stop me
because you think I'm a time traveler.

01:09.180 --> 01:11.141
You mean you aren't?

01:11.683 --> 01:12.767
- Well, I--
- [tires screeching]

01:13.602 --> 01:14.686
- [crashes]
- [glass shatters]

01:16.313 --> 01:17.647
[Takemichi] <i>Kisaki's dead.</i>

01:18.773 --> 01:20.900
<i>That means my fight should be over, right?</i>

01:22.402 --> 01:23.612
<i>But…</i>

01:24.112 --> 01:28.198
<i>for some reason,
since the day Kisaki died,</i>

01:28.199 --> 01:31.369
<i>my hands just won't stop shaking.</i>

01:32.954 --> 01:34.998
[♪ theme song playing]

03:02.001 --> 03:04.044
THE FUNERAL
OF THE LATE EMMA SANO

03:04.045 --> 03:05.254
[chattering]

03:05.255 --> 03:07.339
RECEPTION

03:07.340 --> 03:09.217
[♪ sentimental music playing]

03:30.447 --> 03:31.530
THE LATE EMMA SANO

03:31.531 --> 03:35.033
Thank you for coming. Today we honor
the life of my little sister Emma,

03:35.034 --> 03:36.327
whose life was cut short.

03:37.412 --> 03:42.249
Emma passed away on February 22nd
due to an unforeseen accident.

03:42.250 --> 03:45.210
To all of you
who always looked out for Emma,

03:45.211 --> 03:47.881
and have shown up today
to pay your respects to her,

03:48.465 --> 03:51.175
thank you from the bottom of my heart.

03:51.176 --> 03:53.178
[guests crying]

03:58.600 --> 04:01.227
[Takemichi]
<i>Mikey never lost his composure.</i>

04:09.319 --> 04:10.320
<i>Draken.</i>

04:16.033 --> 04:17.701
I loved Emma so much.

04:18.660 --> 04:19.787
[gasps]

04:22.832 --> 04:24.292
Please forgive me.

04:24.793 --> 04:27.879
In the end, I… couldn't protect her.

04:30.715 --> 04:32.342
[crying]

04:35.386 --> 04:37.262
I see.

04:37.263 --> 04:39.265
So, you loved Emma too.

04:42.060 --> 04:45.103
I'm sure she feels your love, even now.

04:45.104 --> 04:46.898
[crying]

04:59.285 --> 05:00.912
[♪ music continues]

05:05.667 --> 05:09.628
THE LATE SANO

05:09.629 --> 05:10.630
[♪ music ends]

05:20.557 --> 05:21.558
[person] Yo.

05:25.270 --> 05:26.271
Koko.

05:28.356 --> 05:29.607
[footsteps approaching]

05:31.734 --> 05:34.112
I think it's time I walk my own path.

05:39.075 --> 05:41.118
I won't be walking next to you anymore,

05:41.119 --> 05:44.955
so watch your step,
and don't get lost, okay?

05:44.956 --> 05:46.374
[chuckles]

05:47.834 --> 05:49.085
Take care.

05:51.379 --> 05:52.505
Yeah.

05:56.301 --> 05:58.386
Thank you for everything you've done.

05:59.637 --> 06:01.013
Same to you.

06:01.014 --> 06:02.599
See you around, idiot.

06:15.653 --> 06:17.155
- It snowed!
- It snowed!

06:19.616 --> 06:21.618
[both laughing]

06:26.289 --> 06:27.916
[Izana] That's a nasty cut, huh?

06:30.501 --> 06:32.211
Who are you making that for?

06:35.173 --> 06:38.383
Rest in peace, Izana. Goodbye.

06:38.384 --> 06:40.386
[♪ pensive music playing]

06:54.192 --> 06:57.444
[Takemichi] <i>The deaths
of Emma Sano and Izana Kurokawa</i>

06:57.445 --> 07:00.489
<i>were officially recorded as homicides</i>

07:00.490 --> 07:05.161
<i>with Tetta Kisaki as the main culprit
and Shuji Hanma as an accomplice.</i>

07:23.638 --> 07:26.015
[siren wailing]

07:26.599 --> 07:29.059
[cook] Seriously? Another incident?

07:29.060 --> 07:32.020
Feels like the world is getting
more dangerous by the day.

07:32.021 --> 07:34.440
- Check please, mister.
- Sure thing, kid!

07:35.525 --> 07:38.778
What a joke.
Danger's what makes the world exciting.

07:39.404 --> 07:41.030
Thanks for the food, pops!

07:44.325 --> 07:45.576
[engine starts]

07:46.953 --> 07:49.330
Being on the run like this is mad boring.

07:52.291 --> 07:55.962
[Takemichi] <i>To this day,
Shuji Hanma is still a fugitive.</i>

07:56.629 --> 07:58.631
[waves lapping]

08:06.389 --> 08:08.433
That's it. I've decided.

08:11.018 --> 08:12.477
[grunts]

08:12.478 --> 08:14.187
One, two, three, four,

08:14.188 --> 08:17.232
five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten,
11, 12…

08:17.233 --> 08:20.069
[grunts] You see that, Takemitchy?
I've got a new record.

08:21.279 --> 08:23.281
Uh-huh. Nice.

08:23.865 --> 08:25.450
[sighs]

08:27.910 --> 08:29.078
Okay.

08:31.205 --> 08:33.956
Look, man, I know how you feel.

08:33.957 --> 08:37.127
Now that Emma's gone,
and with Izana out of the picture,

08:37.128 --> 08:38.921
- I understand that--
- That's not it.

08:39.505 --> 08:40.629
Huh?

08:40.630 --> 08:44.384
I keep wondering about who Kisaki was.

08:44.385 --> 08:45.636
Hmm.

08:47.930 --> 08:50.141
Thing is, I got it all wrong.

08:50.850 --> 08:53.602
In the end,
Kisaki wasn't a Time Leaper after all.

08:53.603 --> 08:56.354
- What?
- In just one life,

08:56.355 --> 08:58.983
he was able to manipulate
the leaders of Toman,

08:59.484 --> 09:01.110
dispose of his enemies

09:01.611 --> 09:04.489
and climb the ranks
of Japan's top gangs by himself.

09:06.032 --> 09:09.577
How many sleepless nights did it cost him
to accomplish all that?

09:11.245 --> 09:14.373
It's obvious he wasn't the best fighter.

09:15.166 --> 09:17.710
He only needed his brains
to climb to the top.

09:18.336 --> 09:19.711
And I have to respect that.

09:19.712 --> 09:22.047
What the hell are you saying, man?

09:22.048 --> 09:24.925
Who cares how Kisaki
snaked his way up the ranks?

09:24.926 --> 09:26.344
He's still a piece of shit.

09:27.053 --> 09:29.805
Why are you wasting your energy
thinking about him?

09:29.806 --> 09:31.808
That bastard deserved to die.

09:32.391 --> 09:34.102
- I'm just saying--
- Huh?

09:34.852 --> 09:36.979
[screaming]

09:38.064 --> 09:40.733
- Hey! What are you doing?
- [grunts]

09:42.693 --> 09:43.861
Takemitchy!

09:46.030 --> 09:47.907
[gasping]

09:49.700 --> 09:51.201
[gasps]

09:51.202 --> 09:53.245
Why the hell did you do that, you idiot?

09:53.246 --> 09:55.122
- Chifuyu!
- Uh-huh?

09:55.123 --> 09:58.875
[Takemichi] Trust me,
I hate Kisaki just as much as you.

09:58.876 --> 10:00.795
I hate everything he did to us.

10:03.923 --> 10:07.008
And there's no way I'll ever forgive him
for what he did!

10:07.009 --> 10:09.011
[crying]

10:10.471 --> 10:12.430
- [♪ melancholy music playing]
- [no audible dialogue]

10:12.431 --> 10:16.352
But on the day that he died,
he said that it was all for Hina.

10:16.936 --> 10:19.313
And he even told me
that he respected me too!

10:21.065 --> 10:23.359
I didn't know. That's why…

10:24.527 --> 10:27.905
I wish we could have had a real chance
to settle things!

10:29.949 --> 10:31.159
Shit!

10:32.785 --> 10:34.119
Hmm.

10:34.120 --> 10:36.663
You're gonna catch a cold out there,
Takemitchy.

10:36.664 --> 10:37.874
[sniffles]

10:38.583 --> 10:41.460
So, how are you feeling now? Better?

10:42.670 --> 10:46.381
I don't know.
His death just doesn't feel right.

10:46.382 --> 10:49.010
Yeah. I get what you mean.

10:50.344 --> 10:51.929
- [Chifuyu grunts]
- [water splashing]

10:55.349 --> 10:57.268
[Chifuyu]
No matter how much of a villain he was,

10:58.561 --> 11:01.022
losing someone you know is never easy.

11:02.148 --> 11:03.691
[Takemichi] He said he admired me.

11:04.442 --> 11:08.862
Or at least, that's what it sounded
like he was saying in that last fight.

11:08.863 --> 11:13.825
I just don't get it though.
Why would he admire someone like me?

11:13.826 --> 11:16.661
Well, at least he was
a good judge of character.

11:16.662 --> 11:17.663
What?

11:18.581 --> 11:19.790
I didn't say anything.

11:31.260 --> 11:33.095
MUSASHI SHRINE

11:35.264 --> 11:36.556
Hey, Mikey.

11:36.557 --> 11:38.476
Sorry to call you out here.

11:39.393 --> 11:41.187
I wanted to talk to you in private.

11:42.021 --> 11:43.856
I need to ask you something.

11:45.566 --> 11:49.320
I know you're from the future, but…
will you tell me how it all started?

11:52.406 --> 11:53.407
[Takemichi] Sure.

11:55.076 --> 12:00.081
In my original timeline, I was 26 years
old and working part-time jobs to get by.

12:01.040 --> 12:04.000
No matter what I did, nothing worked out.

12:04.001 --> 12:08.505
But if I'm being honest, the real reason
was because I just stopped caring.

12:08.506 --> 12:13.343
In the news, one day I heard about
a yakuza conflict involving Toman,

12:13.344 --> 12:15.805
Hina got caught up in it all
and got killed.

12:16.597 --> 12:21.142
Up until that day, I was a hopeless loser
who basically forgot about her.

12:21.143 --> 12:23.521
She was the only girlfriend I ever had.

12:24.939 --> 12:31.570
And then, on July 4th, 2017,
someone pushed me onto the train tracks.

12:32.363 --> 12:35.156
I thought that was it for me,
but something happened.

12:35.157 --> 12:37.451
I was back in 2005.

12:38.494 --> 12:40.954
It was the day me and my friends
from Mizo Mid

12:40.955 --> 12:43.415
got beat up by Kiyomasa and his crew.

12:43.416 --> 12:46.627
Which was also the day when we were forced
to become his minions.

12:47.169 --> 12:50.756
At first, I thought it was my life
flashing before my eyes.

12:51.966 --> 12:54.010
But somehow, I knew it was different.

12:57.388 --> 13:02.435
And then I ran into Hina, and I knew
there was no way I could just let her die.

13:04.312 --> 13:06.022
That's how all of this began.

13:09.233 --> 13:11.318
[Takemichi] <i>How long had we been talking?</i>

13:11.319 --> 13:14.864
<i>Mikey sat next to me
quietly listening to everything I said.</i>

13:15.781 --> 13:17.700
<i>I think he was letting me get it all out.</i>

13:18.743 --> 13:23.413
<i>As the words trickled out, I found myself
remembering everything that had happened,</i>

13:23.414 --> 13:25.374
<i>and the emotions started flooding back.</i>

13:27.126 --> 13:29.419
[crying]

13:29.420 --> 13:31.922
And I kept going back to fix this, but…

13:32.423 --> 13:35.551
I couldn't save Emma or Baji.

13:36.344 --> 13:38.386
They're dead because of me!

13:38.387 --> 13:39.972
[crying continues]

13:41.599 --> 13:43.017
I'm so sorry.

13:43.768 --> 13:44.810
I'm sorry.

13:45.853 --> 13:49.106
Please forgive me, Mikey! [crying]

13:55.237 --> 13:56.946
I knew you were different.

13:56.947 --> 13:58.324
Huh?

13:59.408 --> 14:01.367
The first time I saw you at the school,

14:01.368 --> 14:05.289
<i>Kiyomasa was beating the shit out of you
in some underground fight.</i>

14:05.915 --> 14:10.001
<i>But no matter how many times he knocked
you on your ass, you stood back up.</i>

14:10.002 --> 14:13.339
<i>That showed me you could carry
the weight of the world on your shoulders.</i>

14:13.964 --> 14:17.218
<i>So you… you're really in middle school?</i>

14:18.886 --> 14:20.471
You haven't changed at all.

14:22.765 --> 14:25.141
You're someone I look up to, Takemitchy.

14:25.142 --> 14:26.936
[wind whistling]

14:31.440 --> 14:33.483
FIRST GENERATION LEADER

14:33.484 --> 14:36.444
I always thought I'd be the one
to bring in a new era.

14:36.445 --> 14:38.029
[creaking]

14:38.030 --> 14:39.031
[gasps]

14:40.491 --> 14:42.284
On your feet, Takemitchy.

14:43.452 --> 14:44.911
Can you hear that?

14:44.912 --> 14:46.288
TOKYO MANJI GANG

14:46.872 --> 14:48.457
The footsteps of change.

14:50.793 --> 14:53.169
You refused to stay down.

14:53.170 --> 14:56.048
And if you ask me,
that's what being in Toman is all about.

14:57.091 --> 14:59.718
Today is a new day for Toman.

15:00.594 --> 15:03.514
[♪ uplifting music playing]

15:11.730 --> 15:13.691
We're all here because of you.

15:18.696 --> 15:20.823
[chuckles] It's finally time.

15:22.241 --> 15:23.450
Listen up, guys!

15:24.118 --> 15:27.453
We had to pay a heavy price,
but we crushed Tenjiku,

15:27.454 --> 15:29.873
and Toman stands on their ashes.

15:29.874 --> 15:34.128
Thanks to you, we are now entering an era
where we're sitting at the top.

15:35.337 --> 15:39.008
Which is why
this is the perfect time to end things.

15:40.050 --> 15:41.051
Huh?

15:41.594 --> 15:46.098
From this day forward,
the Tokyo Manji Gang is disbanded!

15:49.560 --> 15:53.396
From this day forward,
the Tokyo Manji Gang is disbanded!

15:53.397 --> 15:54.856
[gasping]

15:54.857 --> 15:56.566
- What?
- Disbanded?

15:56.567 --> 15:59.527
- [all gasping]
- Mikey, what the hell?

15:59.528 --> 16:01.654
Seriously? Just what are you thinking?

16:01.655 --> 16:03.364
Did he say disbanded?

16:03.365 --> 16:05.910
- There's no way.
- This can't really be the end of Toman.

16:07.369 --> 16:11.080
First Division Captain Takemichi Hanagaki,
to the front.

16:11.081 --> 16:14.292
- Why would he do that?
- After we made it this far?

16:14.293 --> 16:17.337
If we want to change the future,
isn't this the best way?

16:17.338 --> 16:19.505
Let's talk this through. Hold on.

16:19.506 --> 16:23.092
Second Division Captain Takashi Mitsuya,
to the front!

16:23.093 --> 16:25.095
[♪ gentle music playing]

16:28.891 --> 16:29.892
Mikey.

16:30.559 --> 16:33.770
Thank you for your service.
We couldn't have done it without you.

16:33.771 --> 16:36.231
Wait. Hold on just a second.

16:36.232 --> 16:39.485
Third Division Vice Captain
Ryohei Hayashi!

16:41.028 --> 16:43.989
When Pah-chin got locked up,
you did your duty.

16:44.615 --> 16:47.200
You've made us proud, Vice Captain.

16:47.201 --> 16:48.451
Mikey.

16:48.452 --> 16:51.455
Fourth Division Captain Nahoya Kawata!

16:53.040 --> 16:56.626
You always held it down for Toman, Smiley,
so thank you.

16:56.627 --> 16:59.171
Seriously, please stop talking like that.

16:59.755 --> 17:01.589
Mikey, I don't want this.

17:01.590 --> 17:04.549
Fifth Division Captain Yasuhiro Muto!

17:04.550 --> 17:07.178
Even though he's behind bars right now,

17:07.179 --> 17:09.932
he will always be a vital part
of Toman's legacy!

17:11.267 --> 17:17.064
And lastly, Tokyo Manji Gang's
Vice Captain, Ken Ryuguji.

17:23.069 --> 17:27.323
[Ken] Manjiro Sano,
you're such a selfish bastard.

17:27.324 --> 17:30.119
Always acting
like the world revolves around you.

17:30.995 --> 17:35.916
But that charisma is what pulled us in
and kept us following you till the end.

17:36.667 --> 17:39.587
I have no objections
to our leader's decision.

17:40.671 --> 17:44.924
Thank you for everything
you have done for us, Captain!

17:44.925 --> 17:46.302
[sniffles]

17:58.939 --> 18:00.733
Thank you for that, Kenny.

18:01.317 --> 18:02.775
[Toman member] Toman!

18:02.776 --> 18:09.282
[all] Toman! Toman! Toman! Toman!

18:09.283 --> 18:12.118
Even though Toman is disbanding today,

18:12.119 --> 18:15.538
the spirit of Toman will live on
in every one of us.

18:15.539 --> 18:17.041
So lift up your heads!

18:17.625 --> 18:19.083
You must never forget

18:19.084 --> 18:22.378
that Toman's fire
will always be burning in your hearts!

18:22.379 --> 18:25.382
[all cheering]

18:27.509 --> 18:30.970
ONE WEEK LATER, MARCH 15TH, 2006

18:30.971 --> 18:32.973
[bird chirping]

18:36.477 --> 18:38.061
[sighs]

18:38.062 --> 18:39.646
That should do it.

18:39.647 --> 18:41.607
[snickering]

18:43.817 --> 18:45.361
[bird twittering]

18:51.492 --> 18:53.410
It's still hard to accept, man.

18:54.703 --> 18:57.747
So Toman is really ending, isn't it?

18:57.748 --> 18:59.291
Yeah. I guess it is.

18:59.833 --> 19:03.795
But, you know, if I were in Mikey's
position, I'd probably do the same.

19:03.796 --> 19:07.966
'Cause if you think about it,
he's lost the most out of all of us.

19:09.718 --> 19:11.220
- [Chifuyu] Takemitchy?
- Huh?

19:11.804 --> 19:14.138
Now that Toman is done, what's your plan?

19:14.139 --> 19:15.473
Meaning?

19:15.474 --> 19:18.811
[Chifuyu] Well, with Toman disbanded
and Kisaki out of the picture,

19:19.311 --> 19:21.854
there's no reason for you
to stay in the past, is there?

19:21.855 --> 19:23.898
Now that Kisaki's dead,

19:23.899 --> 19:26.610
it's impossible for him to kill Naoto
in the future anymore.

19:28.904 --> 19:33.032
And with Naoto alive,
I should be able to Time Leap again.

19:33.033 --> 19:34.492
Hmm.

19:34.493 --> 19:37.538
This time when I go back,
everything will be better.

19:39.456 --> 19:41.416
Hmm? What's wrong?

19:41.417 --> 19:45.921
After all that happened, everyone
in the past have become like my brothers.

19:46.880 --> 19:47.964
I see.

19:47.965 --> 19:51.426
Man, it's so hard to say goodbye.

19:51.427 --> 19:52.845
It's never easy.

19:53.887 --> 19:55.764
I'm really going to miss everyone.

19:57.808 --> 19:59.726
- Hey, guys!
- [all] Hmm?

19:59.727 --> 20:02.812
We should bury a time capsule
to mark the end of Toman.

20:02.813 --> 20:05.189
- A what now?
- Why a time capsule?

20:05.190 --> 20:06.274
For what reason?

20:06.275 --> 20:07.484
Nice idea.

20:08.694 --> 20:09.820
Let's see…

20:11.321 --> 20:13.489
We should write letters
to our future selves.

20:13.490 --> 20:14.824
Letters?

20:14.825 --> 20:17.369
Hmm… How long should we wait?

20:19.204 --> 20:20.706
How about we open it in 12 years?

20:21.498 --> 20:22.708
That's a pretty long time.

20:26.420 --> 20:28.337
Why did he pick 12 years?

20:28.338 --> 20:30.424
Beats me. Either way, I'm down.

20:31.717 --> 20:33.551
Let's meet back here in a week.

20:33.552 --> 20:35.720
Bring the letter
and something important to you.

20:35.721 --> 20:36.764
Got it?

20:38.682 --> 20:40.224
[Ryohei] So, what'd you bury?

20:40.225 --> 20:43.186
[Takashi] If I told you,
then it would ruin the fun, idiot.

20:43.187 --> 20:45.980
[Souya] Twelve years, huh?
That's a long way off.

20:45.981 --> 20:47.982
I feel like we'll forget
what we put in today.

20:47.983 --> 20:51.360
[Hakkai] Yeah, exactly.
That's the best part of a time capsule.

20:51.361 --> 20:54.113
- [Souya] So you've done this before.
- [Hakkai] Never in my life.

20:54.114 --> 20:56.324
- It's actually a little exciting.
- Yeah.

20:56.325 --> 20:58.410
At least it's something
to look forward to.

21:00.996 --> 21:02.873
Mark it on your calendars.

21:03.457 --> 21:07.627
Twelve years from now on June 19th,
on Toman's founding day,

21:07.628 --> 21:09.338
I wanna see you all back here.

21:10.297 --> 21:12.674
[engine revving]

21:15.219 --> 21:18.347
Hey, man. It means a ton
for you to see me off like this.

21:20.390 --> 21:22.767
This is goodbye, Takemitchy.

21:22.768 --> 21:23.851
Hmm?

21:23.852 --> 21:27.731
The thing is, everyone's got
their own place where they belong.

21:29.024 --> 21:30.691
Your place isn't here, is it?

21:30.692 --> 21:31.693
Hmm?

21:33.195 --> 21:34.278
I know that, but--

21:34.279 --> 21:37.533
Takemitchy, you don't have to worry.

21:38.283 --> 21:40.285
I promise that until we meet again,

21:40.786 --> 21:44.373
I'll protect everyone in Toman,
and I'll keep Hina safe too.

21:47.084 --> 21:48.377
No matter what.

21:49.419 --> 21:51.296
[sniffles] Thanks, Mikey.

21:51.922 --> 21:54.967
Why are you crying?
I know it's hard to say goodbye.

21:55.551 --> 21:57.553
It's time for you to go home now,
Takemitchy.

21:58.637 --> 22:01.931
Hina's been waiting for you
to come back for long enough.

22:01.932 --> 22:02.933
Right.

22:10.983 --> 22:13.485
[♪ theme music playing]

23:40.948 --> 23:42.615
FAIRY TALE REVENGERS - PETIT
#1 "THE RETURN OF MOMOTARO"

23:42.616 --> 23:43.699
<i>- Fairy Tale Revengers.
- Fairy Tale Revengers.</i>

23:43.700 --> 23:46.035
Here's the short rib bowl I promised.

23:46.036 --> 23:47.954
Wow, looks delicious!

23:47.955 --> 23:50.457
It's the perfect reward after the cruise.

23:51.208 --> 23:53.209
- [screaming]
- [laughing]

23:53.210 --> 23:56.253
I hope we can go on more adventures soon.

23:56.254 --> 23:58.422
- Sniff-sniff, sniff-sniff.
- Sniff-sniff, sniff-sniff.

23:58.423 --> 24:01.300
Oh, wow. It smells like heaven, Mikey.

24:01.301 --> 24:03.094
Do you guys want some?

24:03.095 --> 24:04.679
Sure, if you're offering.

24:04.680 --> 24:06.765
- Thank you, Mikey!
- Huh?

24:07.265 --> 24:10.559
Slow down. Leave some for the rest of us.

24:10.560 --> 24:12.853
But I've only had one so far.

24:12.854 --> 24:14.814
- [wings flapping]
- Huh?

24:14.815 --> 24:16.149
Hey, it's them!

24:16.900 --> 24:18.025
When will they learn?

24:18.026 --> 24:20.903
How dare you mess with my short rib bowl!

24:20.904 --> 24:22.530
- Uh-oh.
- Get back here!

24:22.531 --> 24:24.782
- Wait!
- I'm gonna kill you!

24:24.783 --> 24:26.868
TO BE CONTINUED
